1
00:00:00,245 --> 00:00:00,858
Hi there!

2
00:00:00,858 --> 00:00:03,050
Welcome to Shelfie.

3
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:07,790
Rosa's bakery has no website, just a paper menu.

4
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:10,465
An AI assistant just ordered from it,

5
00:00:10,465 --> 00:00:13,483
and Rosa got paid with PayPal.

6
00:00:14,662 --> 00:00:17,687
AI assistants are starting to shop for people.

7
00:00:17,687 --> 00:00:18,975
But they can only buy from

8
00:00:18,975 --> 00:00:21,062
shops with a website store.

9
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,775
In one US survey, nearly half of food

10
00:00:23,775 --> 00:00:26,512
and lodging businesses had no website.

11
00:00:26,512 --> 00:00:28,074
Shelfie is for sellers with

12
00:00:28,074 --> 00:00:30,612
a paper menu and no website.

13
00:00:30,612 --> 00:00:35,392
One photo, and AI shoppers can order and pay.

14
00:00:36,487 --> 00:00:38,087
It works in three steps.

15
00:00:38,087 --> 00:00:39,524
Snap your price list.

16
00:00:39,524 --> 00:00:41,262
AI shoppers order.

17
00:00:41,262 --> 00:00:44,292
And Rosa gets paid on PayPal.

18
00:00:45,612 --> 00:00:46,499
Step one.

19
00:00:46,499 --> 00:00:48,399
Rosa snaps her price list.

20
00:00:48,399 --> 00:00:52,567
Claude, an AI model, reads every item and price.

21
00:00:54,062 --> 00:00:56,437
It only asks about what it wasn't sure of,

22
00:00:56,437 --> 00:00:58,750
like two for seven dollars.

23
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:00,862
Rosa adds her PayPal email,

24
00:01:00,862 --> 00:01:02,674
so the money goes to her.

25
00:01:02,674 --> 00:01:05,812
Then every item goes into PayPal's catalog.

26
00:01:05,812 --> 00:01:08,967
Her shop is live, with photos.

27
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:11,290
Step two.

28
00:01:11,290 --> 00:01:14,628
Every shop gets an agent door: a special address

29
00:01:14,628 --> 00:01:18,353
that AI assistants use to read the menu and order.

30
00:01:18,353 --> 00:01:22,533
It's built on MCP, an open standard.

31
00:01:23,678 --> 00:01:26,528
Here's Claude Code, an AI assistant,

32
00:01:26,528 --> 00:01:29,078
given only the shop's web address.

33
00:01:29,078 --> 00:01:31,253
It finds the agent door by itself,

34
00:01:31,253 --> 00:01:35,983
orders two almond croissants, and gets back a PayPal link.

35
00:01:37,962 --> 00:01:39,837
Shoppers without an assistant can

36
00:01:39,837 --> 00:01:42,162
use the one on the shop page.

37
00:01:42,162 --> 00:01:44,612
This buyer has a nut allergy.

38
00:01:44,612 --> 00:01:46,737
It warns that the almond croissants

39
00:01:46,737 --> 00:01:50,192
contain nuts, then places the order.

40
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:52,395
Step three.

41
00:01:52,395 --> 00:01:54,545
The buyer approves on PayPal.

42
00:01:54,545 --> 00:01:55,770
The money goes straight into

43
00:01:55,770 --> 00:01:58,550
Rosa's own PayPal account.

44
00:02:00,053 --> 00:02:02,778
Her dashboard shows the order as paid.

45
00:02:02,778 --> 00:02:04,178
Claude reads the order from

46
00:02:04,178 --> 00:02:06,503
PayPal and writes her a brief.

47
00:02:06,503 --> 00:02:08,390
It flags the nut allergy,

48
00:02:08,390 --> 00:02:11,258
so she can check before she ships.

49
00:02:12,587 --> 00:02:15,767
And an AI can't change the prices.

50
00:02:16,728 --> 00:02:18,065
Shelfie is for sellers with

51
00:02:18,065 --> 00:02:20,541
a paper menu and no website.

52
00:02:20,541 --> 00:02:23,128
PayPal runs their catalog and checkout,

53
00:02:23,128 --> 00:02:25,053
and pays them directly.

54
00:02:25,053 --> 00:02:28,103
AI reads the menu, lets assistants order,

55
00:02:28,103 --> 00:02:29,640
and writes the brief.

56
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:32,833
For Rosa, paper is now enough.

57
00:02:34,228 --> 00:02:36,308
Thanks for watching!
